<%# locals: (text:, path:, turbo_frame: nil) %>
<%# The "← Back to the list" line above a page's card. One partial so the
    arrow, colour and size match everywhere; the arrow is decoration and hidden
    from screen readers, the text is the link's whole name.

    `turbo_frame: "_top"` is REQUIRED wherever this sits inside a Turbo Frame
    and points at a page with no matching frame: a link inside a frame
    navigates THE FRAME, and Turbo replaces it with "Content missing" rather
    than loading the page. That is exactly what the import wizards' back links
    did before this local existed. %>
<p class="mb-3">
  <%= link_to path, class: "text-sm text-primary underline",
              data: { turbo_frame: turbo_frame }.compact do %>
    <span aria-hidden="true">←</span> <%= text %>
  <% end %>
</p>
